
*Websites:*

- <https://sheldonbrown.com/> -- 
  Well organized information about old bicycles. Indispensible if you are doing a fixie conversion of a vintage bicycle. Sheldon Brown the man died in 2008, but the site is still maintained.

- <https://peter-wiegel.de/> --
  Free fonts, some very interesting historical ones, my favicon is _Altenglisch_.

*Youtube Channels:*

- <https://youtube.com/@BadObsessionMotorsport/> --
I have following since episode 9 of Project Binky, there really is nothing like it on the internet.

- <https://youtube.com/@KnitFactoryImpl/> --
Knitting machines and information on how you can hack them.

- <https://youtube.com/@Clickspring/> --
I have been watching Clickspring almost since its inception, the quality of fabrication is very high, I particularly like his videos on reverse engineering ancient clockmaking techniques.

